   "fp": "2dfc5ea0b80f",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 155,
   "message": "Two of the Security AC-3 mutant scripts only work with GNU sed. The `\\|` alternation in the 'two deleted rules' mutant (line 155) is a GNU basic-regex extension. The one-line block `{h;d}` in the 'rule moved under ## Tests' mutant (line 157) needs a `;` before `}` in BSD sed. On macOS the first matches nothing and the second is a sed error. Either way the mutant file is not the intended mutation, so these checks fail even though base.md is correct. Fix: use two `-e '/.../d'` expressions instead of `\\|`, and write `{h;d;}`. Or state in the test header that the suite needs GNU sed.",
   "original_severity": "minor",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B10",
   "scenario": "Run tests/run-preset-check-tests.sh on macOS with the system sed. The 'two deleted rules' mutant deletes nothing, so security_missing returns '' instead of ' Secrets Crypto' and the check fails. The 'rule moved' mutant hits a BSD sed brace error, which leaves an empty or partial mutant file, so that check also reports a failure. base.md itself is correct in both cases.",
   "severity": "minor"
  }
 ],
